      {
        "id": 122769,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-11T01:01:34.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"arenson9\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/48/1900_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> arenson9:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span>C seems so nonsensical to me that I've had trouble recognizing that people might want this, but if I'm understanding Ronway's response, it's what he wants.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The new option C is what we pretty much have right now. But rather than just Rules, we have the Rules and Gameplay. I'm not so sure why it's so nonsensical, when it has been like this for quite some time now. It's the format I am used to and don't really see a reason to change it.</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
