      {
        "id": 122770,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-11T01:36:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My vote is for each game to have a Rules forum and a \"stuff related to that specific game that isn't actually rules\" forum. So you'd ask about when WotC is going to ship or how to beat Advanced Voss in the SotM non-rules forum (can't think what name to use) and effectively corral the rules questions away from all that.</p><p>Then a generic Sentinels lore forum to ask who that dude with the lizard face is, not game-specific.</p><p>I'm okay with C though, if that's what everyone else wants. Just expressing what would be better for me.</p>",
