      {
        "id": 122771,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-11T01:40:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>arenson9 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>C seems so nonsensical to me that I've had trouble recognizing that people might want this, but if I'm understanding Ronway's response, it's what he wants.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nThe new option C is what we pretty much have right now. But rather than just Rules, we have the Rules and Gameplay. I'm not so sure why it's so nonsensical, when it has been like this for quite some time now. It's the format I am used to and don't really see a reason to change it.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Agreed – option C is what we have now. It seems nonsensical to me because it mixes topics from different games in the same forum, but the majority of the time that I have wanted to read some topics but not others, it's been because I was interested in one game but not all of them. In particular, there was a rush of topics about GSF at one point and I wanted a way to quickly mark them all read, but I couldn't do that as easily as I would have liked because some of the Topics about GSF were in the General forum.</p>",
