      {
        "id": 122773,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-11T03:11:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<div>\n[quote=\"Pydro\"]\n<span>[quote=arenson9]</span>\n</div><div>In particular, there was a rush of topics about GSF at one point and I wanted a way to quickly mark them all read, but I couldn't do that as easily as I would have liked because some of the Topics about GSF were in the General forum.\n[/quote]\n<span>This is also related to the issue of not having to see everything that pops up. RIght now, you can't turn off specific area, rules, or topics. Also, separate forum for forum games that you can not have show up.[/quote]</span>\n</div><div><span>YES! The forum games (and the GSF stuff) are the only things I don't read, and it would be great to have them seperated. BGG has a \"play by forum\" section for each game, but I'm sure we could get away with just one - there's only mostly going to be SotM and Conflict (once it's released) with occasional other things anyway.</span></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Being able to \"ignore\" forums would be really good too.</div>",
